      "question": "A drone equipped with a multispectral sensor flies over a maize field. The resulting data is used to generate a Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) map, which shows a distinct area of low NDVI values (red/yellow). All other factors like water and nutrients are known to be adequate. What is the most logical next step for the farmer?",
